{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "pcache-pgroup-cross-cache-lru-and-limits",
  "title": "PCache PGroup cross-cache LRU, limits, and recycling",
  "status": "subsystem-integrated",
  "admission_ready": true,
  "scope": {
    "rationale": "These source responsibilities jointly own PGroup-wide maximum/minimum/pinned/purgeable accounting, cache registration, recyclable-page LRU membership, cross-cache buffer recycling, soft-create admission, limit enforcement, shrink, and page counts. Native unified mode now shares one intrusive LRU and exact page buffer across caches. The dossier also owns the PCache1/PgHdr1/PGroup fields that directly carry these semantics; static/bulk allocation-only fields remain with their allocation unit.",
